704	/**
705	 * Settles the claim and fixes its due: its amount times the rate of its person's grade in force on its date, in force on the
706	 * claim's date, divided by 100 and rounded to two decimals as the claim rounds (by the sheet's policy date), at least the sheet's floor. With no such rate the due is
707	 * not fixed. A claim a statement bound is settled at its bound figure. The late charge it has gained
708	 * by the sheet's today is frozen in on top. The user who opened the claim may not settle it.
709	 * When a clerk (any user not made a steward) settles a claim whose due is above the sheet's clerk
710	 * limit, it goes to PENDING instead, its due left live until a steward approves or rejects it; a
711	 * due of n/a is within any limit.
